Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CaF MOT Fluorescence Imaging: Camera Comparison", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"77d44e13-ad3e-4b78-9413-0f889da3e9a6"],

Cell["\<\
Analytical noise model and interactive dashboard for imaging the fluorescence \
of a CaF magneto-optical trap (A2Pi1/2 -> X2Sigma+ (0,0) band at 606 nm) with \
five candidate cameras. The notebook is generated and evaluated automatically \
by GenerateCaFComparisonNotebook.wls from the source file CaFCameraNoise.wl. \
Every user-defined symbol is lowerCamelCase; underscores appear only in \
Blank[] patterns.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3ac12f9-ea5c-41ee-afd5-fe7a81ced77d"],

Cell["\<\
Units convention: lengths in mm unless stated, pixel pitches in micrometres, \
times in seconds, charges in electrons, photon fluxes in photons per second \
per square micrometre at the sensor.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c756e78-77c5-44d9-9238-90d827b4c549"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Analytical Noise Engine", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c83f6117-c0be-4f0c-9551-9240e503c030"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
1.1 Optical relay geometry (Thorlabs LA1401-A collector + Comar 29 AF 40 \
imaging lens)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"babf9ae6-1253-4c23-8171-110f62d37bc7"],

Cell["\<\
The MOT sits at the back focal length of the plano-convex singlet (flat side \
facing the MOT), so the fluorescence leaves the collector collimated with a \
beam diameter equal to the illuminated part of that lens (up to 50.8 mm). The \
second lens, a Comar 29 AF 40 achromat (40 mm diameter, EFL 28.6 mm), focuses \
the beam onto the sensor.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d6bfb9d-a349-49ee-8b27-8939f0773ea7"],

Cell["\<\
Two consequences of the real relay, both of which matter for the SNR:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5b641fa-03a6-47c7-a293-c1403c68e111"],

Cell["\<\
(i) Vignetting. The collimated beam is clipped by whichever element has the \
smallest clear aperture; here the 40 mm Comar, not the 2 inch collector, is \
the stop. The accepted solid angle is that of a disc of the limiting radius \
at the working distance, so the geometric efficiency drops from 5.59% \
(unvignetted 2 inch) to 3.69%. Any smaller restriction upstream (a viewport, \
a re-entrant window) would reduce it further: set viewportClearRadius to \
model it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2c16712-a175-4690-837b-b68cfffae9e6"],

Cell["\<\
(ii) Magnification. With two lenses in an infinity relay the magnification is \
M = f2/f1 = 28.6/59.8 = 0.478, so the MOT image is demagnified. This has no \
effect on the total number of collected photons, but it concentrates them \
onto 1/M^2 = 4.4 times fewer pixels, which lowers the integrated read-noise \
and dark-current floor by the same factor, raises the peak electrons per \
pixel (earlier saturation) and coarsens the object-space sampling to \
pixelPitch/M.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7ab248c-b4fb-4561-92b4-354b7e14742f"],

